title Caravan forbear -- a matter its reader says still stands leaves the run that heard it
prompt Autonomous loop -- Standfast on reds, then the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, council rota doc by lap index, condense REMEMBER when a set completes, and send each finished increment as its own signed round.
think Standfast first. The living reds ledger holds rows 96 and 97, both CLOSED and Released, and the earlier ranges are folded to archive. No open agent-closable red stands, so the line is clear for constructive work.
think Council rota by lap index: 1422 logs on disk, 1422 mod 27 = 18, which is context/TWO_ROOMS.md. Deep-read: the checkable room and the vision room, the doorway status tokens, and the one door between them -- a claim crosses by earning a witness, never by sounding proven. It shaped this lap directly: nothing in the new prose claims the impasse is handed on until the witness reads the five bytes back out of the note, outside the run that wrote them.
think The running thread is the Caravan grievance arc, and the last lap's recommend named the crux plainly: allay closed the correspondence one full turn, and nothing yet carries a twice-refused matter anywhere but round again. Two doors stood open -- that constructive rung, and option B, the shared harness. Lindy ranks B higher as infrastructure, yet it is a design call across 91 modules that wants its own word rather than an autonomous rewrite; the finishing edge takes the rung and leaves B named, measured, and one lap closer.
think The name came from the Comlink tendency's three tests. `forbear` is plain English for holding back from something one has the standing to do, it is warm to say, and it collides with nothing in the tree -- grep found zero prior uses across .rye, .rish, and .md.
think The shape follows `owe` rather than `allay`: a note written for a run that has not started. The forbearance is the reader's own five-byte refusal, copied whole into `plan.hold`, so the plan hands on what it was answered with rather than composing a statement of its own.
think One design choice earned its own fold. Every other note in this arc falls with the record beneath it -- a published word falls with the telling it answers, a receipt falls with the debt. A forbearance must not: the whole point is that it outlives the run, so the wire check proves it survives a provisioning AND survives the telling beneath it coming down, and comes down only on the word of the run that inherits it.
obs Both measured runs now read their reader's reply, so `allay` moves identically in each and the judging says so; only the forbearing parts them. Every number beneath stands exactly still.
obs The 70-line ratchet fired again on this rung's own growth -- tell_forbear_tail reached 87 lines -- and was answered rather than carried. Split into tell_forbear_own, which prints the three tiers that close the loop; tail 52 lines, own 42.
obs Three RED paths proven on metal before any GREEN claim, beyond the five folded refusals. A run that hands nothing on is refused by its own tail check; a note carrying the word the reader did not say raises ForbearMisrecorded by name; and a planted control that took the note down after printing GREEN was refused by the witness's own file read at line 190.
obs The ladder meter moved with the rung: 601 folded checks (523 from the fold, 39 each from allay and forbear), carried lines 15,811 against the named ceiling of 22,000 -- about four rungs of headroom now, which is worth naming before it is worth acting on.
loom witness=caravan_forbear_witness modules=92 ladder_checks=1242 distinct_bodies=906 copied_bodies=336 copied_lines=15811 ceiling=22000 folded_checks=601
loom rung=forbear rye_lines=14349 witness_lines=260 unhanded_matters=1->0
file caravan/forbear.rye the rung -- a matter its reader says still stands is handed to the run after, five refusals by name
file tools/caravan_forbear_witness.rish the witness -- the measurement, the five refusals, and the note read back outside the run that wrote it
file caravan/README.md the durable entry for the rung, and the meter's new standing
file tools/caravan_suite_witness.rish registers the rung in the choir
file tools/caravan_ladder_copy_witness.rish the fold count and the carried-line standing move with the ladder
file .gitignore the new note store stays out of the tree
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge names what this rung closed and what stands open
recommend keep-going the arc now corrects a record, carries the correction, hears the answer, records the disagreement, escorts the word, bounds the objection, stands its standing, tells the raiser, reads their reply, carries a live quarrel past the run that heard it, makes the inheriting run answer for it, lets its holder close it, dates it, reads that age aloud, puts a long-standing one before a third hand, reads back what that hand made of it, makes the plan answer that finding on the record, carries the plan's own concession forward, makes the run that inherits it meet it, makes that meeting say what it found, carries that finding home to the reader who won it, reads what that reader makes of it, takes the matter up again when they say it falls short, makes the run that inherits that reopening look, carries what the second look found home, reads whether that finally settles it, and now hands the impasse on when it does not. So the loop closes: the correspondence no longer goes round forever, and the next question is what the run that INHERITS a forbearance does with it -- open it fresh, or read it as the boundary of what this pair of hands can settle and carry it somewhere else entirely. Beside it option B stands measured and one lap closer: 15,811 carried lines and two named limits, both of which a harness running a rung's checks against its own report and its own wire would take, and the headroom is now four rungs rather than six.
